[00:05.37] Farewell the temple master's bells
[00:11.60] His kiosk and his black worm seed
[00:17.33] Courtship solely of his word
[00:22.42] With Eden guaranteed
[00:27.62] For now Prince Rupert's tears of glass
[00:33.59] Make saffron sabbath eyelids bleed
[00:39.20] Scar the sacred tablet of wax
[00:44.45] On which the Lizards feed
[00:50.96] Wake your reason's hollow vote
[00:56.55] Wear your blizzard season coat
[01:02.05] Burn a bridge and burn a boat
[01:07.58] Stake a Lizard by the throat
[01:12.33] Go Polonius or kneel
[01:17.72] The reapers name their harvest dawn
[01:23.73] All your tarnished devil's spoons
[01:28.89] Will rust beneath our corn
[01:34.34] Now bears Prince Rupert's garden roam
[01:40.00] Across his rain tree shaded lawn
[01:45.72] Lizard bones become the clay
[01:51.04] And there a Swan is born
[01:57.49] Wake your reasons' hollow vote
[02:02.97] Wear your blizzard season coat
[02:08.35] Burn a bridge and burn a boat
[02:13.80] Stake a Lizard by the throat
[02:18.90] 
[02:39.64] Gone soon Piepowder's moss-weed court
[02:45.68] Round which upholstered Lizards sold
[02:51.56] Visions to their leaden flock
[02:56.76] Of rainbows' ends and gold
[03:01.64] Now tales Prince Rupert's peacock brings
[03:07.96] Of walls and trumpets thousand fold
[03:13.65] Prophets chained for burning masks
[03:18.71] And reels of dream unrolled
[03:25.11] 
[12:04.27] Night enfolds her cloak of holes
[12:09.17] Around the river meadow
[12:15.22] Old moon-light stalks by broken ploughs
[12:20.59] Hides spokeless wheels in shadow
[12:27.95] Sentries lean on thorn wood spears
[12:32.52] Blow on their hands, stare eastwards
[12:41.34] Burnt with dream and taut with fear
[12:45.91] Dawn's misty shawl upon them
[12:52.38] Three hills apart great armies stir
[12:57.90] Spit oat and curse as day breaks
[13:05.10] Forming lines of horse and steel
[13:09.79] By even yards, march forward
[13:21.43] 